# `.agentic-sdlc/` carries no machine-local activation state any more. The transactional
# activation engine that produced receipts, transaction journals, plane pointers, and
# `repo.toml` is deleted, so the former `.agentic-sdlc/receipts/`, `.agentic-sdlc/transactions/`,
# and `.agentic-sdlc/plane.*.json` rules would ignore paths nothing writes. Repository
# activation is now a reviewed diff written by `instruction-generator.py apply`, and its
# evidence is the Git history of the files it changed.
#
# `.agentic-sdlc/rightsize/` remains deliberately VISIBLE to Git: rendered recommendation
# artifacts a reader may commit. Do not "tidy" it into an ignore rule — hiding it would let the
# same file behave differently tracked versus untracked.
